 (10, 'HABIBA', '1:35', 'Milestone 1 feedback', 'From your Milestone 1 feedback we changed the design: a security pipeline in front of every module, an Admin actor, and the core flow first. Every change has an ID in the change log of the SRS and SDD. Karim.'),
 (22, 'KARIM', '1:54', 'Three looks', 'Thank you, Habiba. The heart of Closet: choose an occasion, and Closet builds three complete looks from the pieces that are really available, for today’s weather, each with a match percentage and the reason. You can change one piece, save, wear or reject it. And each look has Virtual Try-On — Youssef.'),
 (24, 'YOUSSEF', '2:19', 'Virtual Try-On · pick a piece', 'Thanks, Karim. Virtual Try-On is image-based — no camera, no AR. From a look you choose one piece: a top, a jacket or a dress. <i>[Click.]</i>'),
 (24, 'YOUSSEF', '2:33', 'Virtual Try-On · the base photo', 'Then your base photo: one full-body photo you take once while setting up Closet, and use to try on every piece. You agree to a short notice first. <i>[Click.]</i>'),
 (24, 'YOUSSEF', '2:48', 'Virtual Try-On · creating', 'Our server — never the browser — sends the photo and the piece to the AI try-on service; the key stays on the server. <i>[Click.]</i>'),
 (24, 'YOUSSEF', '3:01', 'Virtual Try-On · the result', 'And the result comes back: save it, try another piece, or go back to the outfit. This picture is an illustration of the result we are building: today the demo provider returns your photo unchanged, and in Sprint 2, with the live AI key, the piece is drawn on you like this.'),
 (15, 'YOUSSEF', '3:24', 'The live closet', 'Now let us show you all of this live. <i>[Click LIVE DEMO — the app opens in the browser. LIVE DEMO, 2 min 40 s — see the demo steps. If the app does not open, click BACKUP RECORDING. Then back to the slides.]</i>'),
 (52, 'BASHAR', '6:08', 'Use case diagram v2.0', 'Thank you. Behind the demo: our use case diagram, version 2.0 — the User on the left, the Admin bottom right, the external services on the right. Colours: rose for the key use cases, green for «extend», yellow for «include», blue for the try-on details, lilac for the Admin. <i>[Click.]</i>'),
 (53, 'BASHAR', '6:32', 'Zoom · account, closet, shopping', 'At the top: sign-in, the profile and the closet; the duplicate warning extends adding a piece, and deleting a damaged piece extends the shopping list. <i>[Click.]</i>'),
 (54, 'BASHAR', '6:46', 'Zoom · outfits and Virtual Try-On', 'The heart: Get Outfit Recommendations includes availability and weather, and is extended by changing a piece, saving, rejecting — and Virtual Try-On, which includes the base photo. <i>[Click.]</i>'),
